1
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,897
YAMOO! YAMOO! YAMOO! YAMOO!

2
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:29,860
YAMOO!

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,620
Your moves!

4
00:01:02,860 --> 00:01:03,690
Hey, Joey.

5
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:05,700
Earth to Joey.

6
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:07,980
Hey, are you in there?

7
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:09,022
It's your turn.

8
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:13,740
Oh, isn't he cute when he's thinking?

9
00:01:14,020 --> 00:01:14,860
Hey, Tristan.

10
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:17,417
Yugi is teaching me how
to play duel monsters.

11
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:18,559
Drooling monsters?

12
00:01:18,740 --> 00:01:20,340
Duel monsters, you nimrod.

13
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:22,230
Sheesh.

14
00:01:22,313 --> 00:01:23,777
They've been at it for hours.

15
00:01:23,860 --> 00:01:27,197
Joey's starting to get the hang of
the game, but Yugi's like an expert.

16
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:28,220
Okay, Yugi.

17
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:30,040
It's time to duel.

18
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:33,677
See, each card has an attack
number and a defense number.

19
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:36,917
First player to eliminate their
opponent's life points wins the duel.

20
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,900
Pretty good move, huh, Yu-Gi?

21
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:43,960
Yep, pretty good move,
but not good enough.

22
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:46,070
What?

23
00:01:46,180 --> 00:01:47,460
Thanks a lot.

24
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:50,440
A card that powerful totally wipes me out.

25
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:52,800
Whoa, you stink at this game, Joey.

26
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:54,540
You did fine, Joey.

27
00:01:54,760 --> 00:01:56,237
I just have better cards.

28
00:01:56,320 --> 00:02:00,417
See, my grandpa owns a game shop,
and I get all my best cards from him.

29
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:01,760
Your own game shop?

30
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:03,097
What are we waiting for?

31
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:04,600
Let's go! Okay.

32
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,294
Maybe I can even get my grandpa to
show us this super rare card he's got.

33
00:02:09,540 --> 00:02:10,370
Rare card?

34
00:02:10,453 --> 00:02:13,809
Could they have found the card
that I've been searching for?

35
00:02:15,660 --> 00:02:16,490
Grandpa?

36
00:02:16,573 --> 00:02:17,403
I'm home.

37
00:02:17,780 --> 00:02:19,637
And I see you've brought company.

38
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:23,417
Gramps, could you show my friends
your awesome super rare card?

39
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:24,440
Rare card?

40
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:25,521
My special card?

41
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:27,150
Hmm.

42
00:02:28,220 --> 00:02:29,120
Please, please.

43
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:30,090
Ready, please?

44
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:31,630
Hmm.

45
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:33,310
Ha, ha.

46
00:02:33,393 --> 00:02:34,440
How can I refuse?

47
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:36,427
You kids are in for a treat.

48
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:38,517
I don't take this card out too often.

49
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:39,430
Ready?

50
00:02:39,513 --> 00:02:40,343
Here it is.

51
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:43,440
The Blue Eyes White Dragon.

52
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:46,719
So rare, so powerful, I
never let it leave my hands.

53
00:02:47,780 --> 00:02:48,610
Awesome.

54
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:50,010
Hmm.

55
00:02:50,093 --> 00:02:51,737
Doesn't look all that special to me.

56
00:02:51,820 --> 00:02:54,120
Ah, this card is priceless.

57
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:56,237
There are only four of
them in all the world.

58
00:02:56,320 --> 00:02:58,397
Speaking of priceless, I'm ready to trade.

59
00:02:58,480 --> 00:02:59,640
Not for this card.

60
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:01,330
Huh?

61
00:03:01,413 --> 00:03:02,347
No, I didn't mean that card.

62
00:03:02,820 --> 00:03:06,114
I meant show me some other
cool cards to get me started.

63
00:03:08,020 --> 00:03:09,314
Hello, can I help you?

64
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:12,780
If you can't, it certainly
wouldn't surprise me.

65
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:16,460
Sato Kaiba! Kaiba!

66
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:18,937
Doesn't he have a big
fancy company to run?

67
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:20,437
What's he doing down here?

68
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:24,137
Not that it's any of your business,
but I came to see the card.

69
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:26,220
Hey, are you into Duel Monsters 2?

70
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:27,261
This is perfect.

71
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:29,677
Maybe we could all duel together sometime.

72
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:30,900
Me? Duel you?

73
00:03:31,180 --> 00:03:34,017
I would have more of a
challenge playing solitaire.

74
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:34,930
What?

75
00:03:35,013 --> 00:03:37,477
I am the number one ranked
duelist in the country and

76
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:40,560
the favorite to win the
Duel Monsters Championship.

77
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:43,917
You wouldn't last two
minutes in a duel against me.

78
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,020
Ooh, I'm shaking.

79
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:47,977
Maybe you'd like to settle this
with fists instead of cards.

80
00:03:48,060 --> 00:03:49,497
Whoa, take it easy, Joey.

81
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:52,200
But, Yu-Gi, Kaiba's asking for it.

82
00:03:52,340 --> 00:03:55,458
Now, does this shop have
any worthwhile cards or not?

83
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:02,900
Hey, can it be the Blue-Eyes
White Dragon in a dump like this?

84
00:04:03,940 --> 00:04:06,640
It is the card I've been searching for.

85
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:09,177
Well, enough window shopping.

86
00:04:09,260 --> 00:04:11,789
Is there anything else
I can help you with?

87
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:20,040
Listen to me, old man.

88
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:24,614
Give me your Blue-Eyes White Dragon
card and I'll trade you all of these.

89
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:28,120
Ah, nice.

90
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:29,340
But no thanks.

91
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:32,650
Fine.

92
00:04:32,733 --> 00:04:34,557
If you won't trade, maybe you'll sell it.

93
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:35,537
Name your price.

94
00:04:35,620 --> 00:04:37,208
I can pay anything you ask.

95
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:38,960
I'm sure you could.

96
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:42,797
But this card is worth more to
me than you could ever offer.

97
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:45,757
Not because of its power,
or because it's so rare,

98
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:47,899
but because of what it means to me.

99
00:04:48,300 --> 00:04:51,400
This card was given to
me by a dear friend.

100
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:54,760
And so I treasure this
card as I do that friend.

101
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:58,838
So parting with it is
completely out of the question.

102
00:04:59,980 --> 00:05:00,810
No.

103
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:05,082
You'd feel the same even if it
were a common card, right, Grandpa?

104
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:06,110
Exactly.

105
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:10,520
You see, this precious card
has bonded with my heart. Fine.

106
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:12,859
I've heard enough of your nonsense.

107
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:14,540
Senile old fool.

108
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:20,537
Hard in the cards. Ridiculous.

109
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:22,840
These cards are all about power.

110
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:27,860
And one way or another, his Blue
Eyes White Dragon card will be mine.

111
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:35,990
Gentlemen,

112
00:05:36,073 --> 00:05:39,297
there's a little something I'd like
you to pick up for me at the game shop.

113
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:40,760
Gladly, Master Kaiba.

114
00:05:47,540 --> 00:05:48,370
Good morning.

115
00:05:50,660 --> 00:05:53,880
My master Seto Kaiba
challenges you to a duel.

116
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:56,040
You will come with us now.

117
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:58,660
And if I were to decline?

118
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:02,200
I'm afraid I must insist.

119
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:05,340
Young Kaiba doesn't understand,

120
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:08,957
but I'll teach him a lesson
about the heart of the cards.

121
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:10,817
Man, I hope he has some cool cards today.

122
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:11,730
Me too.

123
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:14,809
Okay, Gramps, we're
back to get more cards.

124
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,520
Hey, hey, Gramps.

125
00:06:16,720 --> 00:06:17,940
Grandpa, I'm home.

126
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:20,000
Maybe he went out.

127
00:06:20,620 --> 00:06:23,444
Maybe, but why would he
leave the door unlocked?

128
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:29,540
Hello? Game shop? Ah, Yugi. Perfect.

129
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:30,950
Kaiba?

130
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:34,437
Your grandfather's here visiting,
but he's not feeling well.

131
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:38,420
Why don't you come by my
office and pick him up? Kaiba?

132
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:40,129
What have you done, Kaiba?

133
00:06:54,420 --> 00:06:55,250
Grandpa!

134
00:06:55,333 --> 00:06:56,163
Grandpa!

135
00:06:56,246 --> 00:06:57,076
Are you okay?

136
00:06:57,400 --> 00:06:58,840
Yogi, I failed.

137
00:06:59,180 --> 00:07:04,560
I wanted to teach that boy Kaiba a lesson
about the heart of the cards, but I lost.

138
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:06,830
Grandpa!

139
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:11,640
How's the old man feeling,
hmm? Kaiba! You sleaze!

140
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:12,857
What have you done to him?

141
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:14,469
We had a duel, that's all.

142
00:07:14,580 --> 00:07:17,337
With each of us putting up our
most valuable card as the prize.

143
00:07:17,420 --> 00:07:20,457
But I guess playing against
a champion like myself

144
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:23,260
was just too much
stimulation for the old fool

145
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:26,673
Kaiba you should be ashamed of yourself.

146
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:30,660
It was fair and look at the sweet prize.

147
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:31,710
I won

148
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:36,320
Grandpa's most treasured card Yes,

149
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:39,077
the blue-eyes white dragon
is a rare and powerful

150
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:42,340
card and this one will
never be used against me

151
00:07:43,020 --> 00:07:46,220
My blue-eyes white dragon my treasure

152
00:07:47,440 --> 00:07:49,140
Grandpa, hold on!

153
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:51,560
How could you do such a thing?

154
00:07:51,780 --> 00:07:52,800
Yugi, here.

155
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:55,520
Take this. Huh? Grandpa?

156
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:57,360
I built this deck.

157
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:59,640
I put my soul in these cards.

158
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:03,960
And I taught you everything
I know, Yugi. Take them.

159
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:06,318
Take my cards and teach him respect.

160
00:08:06,540 --> 00:08:09,658
Teach Kaiba respect for the
heart of the cards, Yugi.

161
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:11,637
But Grandpa, you need help.

162
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:13,197
I've got to get you to a doctor.

163
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:14,574
Sounds like an excuse.

164
00:08:14,980 --> 00:08:17,509
Your friends can care
for your grandfather.

165
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:21,840
While you and I duel, unless
you're afraid. Take him, Yugi!

166
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:27,860
We could take care of your grandpa
while you take care of creepy Kaiba.

167
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:31,117
Teach that rich spoiled brat
what a real duel's all about.

168
00:08:31,200 --> 00:08:33,660
For your grandpa, Yugi. I don't know.

169
00:08:34,340 --> 00:08:35,170
Trust me,

170
00:08:35,253 --> 00:08:38,137
you're like the best player I've ever
seen and you've got the Millennium Puzzle.

171
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:39,540
You can do this, Yugi.

172
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:41,120
I know you can.

173
00:08:41,380 --> 00:08:42,300
We all do.

174
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,837
Okay, Grandpa, I'll do it.

175
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:47,700
I know you will, my boy.

176
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:50,440
Everyone, put your hands together.

177
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:52,956
And I'll mark us with a special sign.

178
00:08:53,980 --> 00:08:55,240
What gives, Taya?

179
00:08:55,780 --> 00:08:57,457
It's a symbol of our friendship.

180
00:08:57,540 --> 00:09:01,057
So when Yugi's dueling, no matter how tough
it gets, he'll know that he's not alone.

181
00:09:01,140 --> 00:09:02,964
We're all right there with him.

182
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:11,557
Joey, Tristan and I will take
Yugi's grandpa to the hospital.

183
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:13,877
Why don't you get back in
there and cheer Yugi on?

184
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:16,180
Okay, take good care of him, Taya.

185
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:19,500
I designed this virtual stadium myself.

186
00:09:19,940 --> 00:09:20,940
Impressive, hmm?

187
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:22,457
I think you'll agree.

188
00:09:22,540 --> 00:09:24,660
It adds a bit more life to the game.

189
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:27,860
We each begin with 2,000 life points.

190
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:29,984
First player to hit zero loses.

191
00:09:30,460 --> 00:09:32,480
Are you ready to play, Runt?

192
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:34,820
Playtime is over, Kaiba!

193
00:09:38,980 --> 00:09:40,500
Yu-Gi-Oh!

194
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:56,120
Yu-Gi-Oh!

195
00:09:58,300 --> 00:09:59,477
What the...

196
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:04,060
Now, Kaiba, prepare yourself,
because it's time to duel.

197
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,480
Virtual system's ready.

198
00:10:12,700 --> 00:10:14,080
So let's begin.

199
00:10:14,880 --> 00:10:17,760
I attack with the mighty Hitatsumi giant.

200
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:19,840
Brace yourself, Yugi.

201
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:22,256
You've never dueled like this before.

202
00:10:23,620 --> 00:10:24,450
Huh?

203
00:10:24,533 --> 00:10:26,637
This brought the monster
on the card to life.

204
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:28,340
It's my virtual simulator.

205
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:31,720
It creates lifelike holograms
of every duel monster.

206
00:10:31,980 --> 00:10:34,097
So this is how you beat my grandfather.

207
00:10:34,180 --> 00:10:36,720
Well, now it's my turn.

208
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:41,040
I call on the winged dragon,
guardian of the fortress.

209
00:10:45,820 --> 00:10:47,180
Whoa, monsters?

210
00:10:48,140 --> 00:10:49,320
Real monsters?

211
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:52,420
Fireball attack!

212
00:10:58,220 --> 00:11:01,180
Big Brother, are you all right?

213
00:11:01,980 --> 00:11:04,140
All right! Go, Yugi!

214
00:11:05,580 --> 00:11:07,840
Well played, Yugi, for a beginner.

215
00:11:08,140 --> 00:11:10,022
But how will you deal with this?

216
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:16,500
Soggy the Dark Clown, but that card
has hardly any attack strength.

217
00:11:17,180 --> 00:11:23,160
True, your Winged Dragon's attack is
1,400, while my Dark Clown's is only 600.

218
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:26,397
But if I combine it with this card...

219
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:27,980
A magic card!

220
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:29,550
Exactly.

221
00:11:29,780 --> 00:11:31,545
The Negative Energy Generator.

222
00:11:31,640 --> 00:11:34,280
It multiplies my
monster's attack by three.

223
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:39,380
Dark Clown, attack with Dark Light!

224
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:50,320
As you can see, combining
cards can be very effective.

225
00:11:51,380 --> 00:11:52,360
He's good.

226
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:54,597
He knows every aspect of this game.

227
00:11:54,680 --> 00:11:57,320
But my grandpa put all
his gaming knowledge,

228
00:11:57,460 --> 00:11:59,989
his whole heart, into
assembling this deck.

229
00:12:00,540 --> 00:12:03,820
I have to believe that it
holds some secret strategy.

230
00:12:04,660 --> 00:12:05,920
This card is useless.

231
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:08,057
I can't beat the Dark Clown with this.

232
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:09,677
I'll have to use a different monster.

233
00:12:09,760 --> 00:12:10,701
In defense mode.

234
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:15,135
The monster will be sacrificed, but
my overall life points will be safe.

235
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:17,800
Dark Light Attack!

236
00:12:23,060 --> 00:12:24,236
Hang in there, Yugi!

237
00:12:32,300 --> 00:12:35,594
You're not faring any better
than the old man did, Yugi.

238
00:12:36,820 --> 00:12:40,520
Your deck is just as weak and
feeble as your grandfather.

239
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:45,041
My grandpa is a great man and a
better duelist than you'll ever be.

240
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:49,258
He entrusted me with his cards, and
I can feel his heart in this deck.

241
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:54,040
I doubt you have that kind of
faith in your cards, Kaiba. What?

242
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:57,480
But I believe in my grandpa's deck.

243
00:13:02,600 --> 00:13:06,460
And my faith rewards me with
Gaia, the Fierce Knight,

244
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:09,580
with a destructive power of 2300.

245
00:13:21,540 --> 00:13:22,880
Way to go, Yugi!

246
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:25,520
All right, Kaiba, your move.

247
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:28,840
Ha, this'll be over sooner than you think.

248
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:34,280
I call on the blue-eyes white dragon.

249
00:13:37,020 --> 00:13:38,500
Huh? No way.

250
00:13:39,020 --> 00:13:39,850
Impossible.

251
00:13:39,933 --> 00:13:42,297
We all watch Kaiba tear that card in half.

252
00:13:42,380 --> 00:13:43,210
Surprised?

253
00:13:43,293 --> 00:13:48,121
Did you think your grandfather was the only
one to possess a blue-eyes white dragon?

254
00:13:56,680 --> 00:13:59,420
Ha, your fierce knight is destroyed.

255
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:04,640
Faith or no faith, you will fall
before my superior monsters, Yugi.

256
00:14:05,620 --> 00:14:08,720
Power is what this game
is all about, you fool.

257
00:14:09,340 --> 00:14:12,800
Faith is for losers, like
your pathetic grandfather.

258
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:14,377
In your entire deck,

259
00:14:14,460 --> 00:14:18,695
there's not a single card that can
stand up to a blue-eyes white dragon.

260
00:14:18,780 --> 00:14:21,100
So what hope do you have against two?

261
00:14:23,780 --> 00:14:26,300
Why don't you just admit defeat, Yugi?

262
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:33,940
Don't give up, Yugi.

263
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:36,380
I won't give up.

264
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:38,191
Grandpa's counting on me.

265
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:41,100
A magic card.

266
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:43,660
Swords of Revealing Light!

267
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:47,480
It stops all monsters on
the field for three turns.

268
00:14:48,620 --> 00:14:49,880
How desperate.

269
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:54,560
What possible good will a
three-turn delay do you? He's right.

270
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:55,760
What do I do?

271
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:58,397
I can't figure out what
to do with these cards.

272
00:14:58,480 --> 00:15:00,304
They're just a bunch of pieces.

273
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:04,000
How can I use them to
battle an expert like Kaiba?

274
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:08,398
For someone claiming to have faith,
you're giving up too easily, Yugi.

275
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,706
Listen, sometimes the
cards are like a puzzle.

276
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:15,940
You have to put all the different
pieces in their proper place.

277
00:15:16,720 --> 00:15:19,080
Ah, like the Millennium Puzzle? Exactly.

278
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:21,800
Each piece helps build a greater entity.

279
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:23,990
Grandpa!

280
00:15:24,780 --> 00:15:28,560
Like the pieces of a
puzzle, Yugi. Remember!

281
00:15:29,420 --> 00:15:30,250
Puzzle?

282
00:15:30,333 --> 00:15:32,121
When are the cards like a puzzle?

283
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:34,097
Wait, Grandpa once said...

284
00:15:34,180 --> 00:15:38,360
Dual Monsters contains only one
unstoppable monster, Exodia.

285
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:42,367
But he can only be summoned by
drawing all five special cards.

286
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:46,680
A feat that to this very day
no one has ever accomplished.

287
00:15:48,420 --> 00:15:51,880
Quit your stalling, Yu-Gi, or
you will forfeit the match.

288
00:15:52,060 --> 00:15:53,280
I never forfeit.

289
00:15:56,220 --> 00:15:57,867
Another piece of the puzzle.

290
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:59,277
Draw any card you like.

291
00:15:59,360 --> 00:16:00,517
It won't change a thing.

292
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:03,017
My dragons may be frozen
for another two turns,

293
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:05,571
but my new monster is under no such spell.

294
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:09,980
The Judge Man, with an
attack power of 2,200.

295
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:16,978
I can attack with the Dark Magician,

296
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:21,318
but he won't stand a chance once
Kaiba's dragons are free of my spell.

297
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:24,280
Dark Magician, attack!

298
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:31,460
Your Judge Man falls.

299
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:36,840
Oh, a sacrifice that doesn't even faze me.

300
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:39,119
And though neither dragon can move.

301
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:45,100
For one more turn, my next card is
the third Blue-Eyes White Dragon.

302
00:16:48,820 --> 00:16:50,620
Now my dragon, attack!

303
00:16:57,980 --> 00:17:01,020
So tell me, Yugi, how's your faith now?

304
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:05,580
On my next turn, all three Blue-Eyes
White Dragons are free to attack.

305
00:17:05,940 --> 00:17:08,780
This game's over no
matter what card you draw.

306
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:19,937
you can't possibly stand against my three
blue eyes white dragons it's over yuki

307
00:17:20,020 --> 00:17:26,077
you were never a match for me don't
listen yuki kaiba had three blue eyes all

308
00:17:26,160 --> 00:17:30,517
along he only wanted grandpa's card so
it couldn't be used against him my only

309
00:17:30,600 --> 00:17:35,247
chance now is to assemble all the pieces
of exodia but The odds are against me.

310
00:17:35,740 --> 00:17:37,387
I don't think I can do this.

311
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,060
The deck, it senses my doubt.

312
00:17:44,460 --> 00:17:45,860
Don't lose focus, Yugi.

313
00:17:46,040 --> 00:17:47,040
Don't lose faith.

314
00:17:47,320 --> 00:17:48,150
Concentrate.

315
00:17:49,300 --> 00:17:50,660
Our friendship symbol.

316
00:17:54,780 --> 00:17:56,740
Yugi, we're right here with you.

317
00:17:57,140 --> 00:17:59,337
Yugi, you've got to believe in yourself.

318
00:17:59,420 --> 00:18:00,250
You can do it.

319
00:18:00,333 --> 00:18:01,673
Just kick Kaiba's butt.

320
00:18:01,980 --> 00:18:02,810
They're right.

321
00:18:02,893 --> 00:18:05,817
I've got to believe in the cards
like my friends believe in me.

322
00:18:05,900 --> 00:18:09,380
Draw your last pathetic card
so I can end this, Yugi.

323
00:18:09,940 --> 00:18:13,260
My grandpa's deck has no
pathetic cards, Kaiba.

324
00:18:13,640 --> 00:18:16,020
But it does contain...

325
00:18:16,740 --> 00:18:18,640
the unstoppable Exodia.

326
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:20,590
Impossible!

327
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:23,880
I've assembled all five special cards.

328
00:18:24,040 --> 00:18:25,840
All five pieces of the puzzle.

329
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:37,720
Exodia, it's not possible.

330
00:18:38,080 --> 00:18:40,240
No one's ever been able to call him.

331
00:18:42,340 --> 00:18:43,860
Exodia, obliterate!

332
00:18:54,960 --> 00:18:56,220
You did it!

333
00:18:56,420 --> 00:18:57,360
Yugi, you won!

334
00:18:57,740 --> 00:18:58,860
This can't be.

335
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:00,377
My brother never loses.

336
00:19:00,460 --> 00:19:05,180
You play only for power, Kaiba,
and that is why you lost.

337
00:19:05,420 --> 00:19:09,479
But if you put your heart in the
game, there is nothing you can't do.

338
00:19:09,860 --> 00:19:11,180
But... but how?

339
00:19:11,520 --> 00:19:13,320
How could I have lost to him?

340
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:18,540
Kaiba, if you truly want
to know, open your mind!

341
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:23,760
There, Kaiba.

342
00:19:24,080 --> 00:19:25,980
Maybe now you will begin to see.

343
00:19:29,460 --> 00:19:32,280
Grandpa's awake Yugi won

344
00:19:34,380 --> 00:19:35,210
Mr.

345
00:19:35,293 --> 00:19:39,907
Pegasus, sir Seto Kaiba, our uncontested
champion He's been defeated in a duel,

346
00:19:40,100 --> 00:19:42,300
sir By someone named Yugi

347
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:15,220
Oh, my God.
